From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:10:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: panorama auto columns widen on large windows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

One minimum cannot suit a folded phone and an unfolded window. Under
600 dp the minimum is 112 dp, which keeps a tall cover on three columns.
At 600 dp and above it is 140 dp, so a wide window does not add columns
of small covers.

The tier is the grid's own width: lane area plus horizontal content
padding (16 dp in portrait, scaffold insets plus PaddingValues(8.dp)).
That is the pane in split-screen or a freeform window, so configuration
screen width is not read. Lane count stays staggeredLaneCountAdaptive,
lanes = (available + 4) / (min + 4), available = window width - 16.

Pura X Max folded portrait is about 459 dp and lands on 3 columns;
unfolded landscape is about 939 dp and lands on 6. vivo X100 Pro
portrait is 360 and 420 dp, both 3 columns. The width table is
360/420/459 → 3, 664/672 → 4, 800 → 5, 933/939 → 6. Just below the
breakpoint, 599 dp still uses 112 dp; 600 dp uses 140 dp.

PanoramaColumns.Tiered is its own subtype so Adaptive stays the
single-minimum StaggeredGridCells.Adaptive rule. The breakpoint is a
grid-width input that Adaptive does not take, and the measure branch
has to handle it.

与 anikku-harmony 0036 同源。
